      "created_at": "2019-05-21T09:00:16Z",
      "updated_at": "2019-05-21T09:00:16Z",
      "body": "According to GDPR (General Data Protection Regulation) all EU citizens and residents have the right to be forgotten.  These GDPR-regulations also apply to digital companies outside of the EU https://gdpr.eu/companies-outside-of-europe/  \r\n\r\nCurrently there seems to be no procedure, and no documentation, in Bountyscore on how to delete all account-related information. \r\n\r\nSolutions: \r\n1. As a minimum: describe in the FAQ or documentation, how to ask for deletion of all user-related data + install a procedure to execute these requests + give feedback during the process and provide a final confirmation.  \r\n2. Provide an automated procedure (ex. in the account-section - as implemented on GitHub: https://github.com/settings/admin ) for erasure of all data related to a user  \r\n\r\nMore info on these legal requirements:\r\n- https://gdpr.eu/article-17-right-to-be-forgotten/\r\n- https://gdpr.eu/companies-outside-of-europe/ \r\n\r\nThanks for looking into this issue, not only for your EU-visitors. This feature is a minimum for a website that records sensitive user-related information.  \r\n\r\nAs long as this is not resolved, I would advise you on excluding visitors (both citizens and residents) from EU from using your services.   \r\n\r\n",
      "author_association": "NONE",
